..." diagnostic precedent), (1) once per mode (re)construction --
"vivace: deinterlace enabled, mode=%d (%s)" -- confirming the menu
selection actually reached this code and which concrete filter
(yadif/bwdif) it picked, and (2) once per (re)construction, the first
time the filter graph actually produces an output frame -- "vivace:
deinterlace producing filtered output frames" -- confirming frames are
genuinely flowing through the avfilter graph, not silently failing every
call. A new `VideoRenderer::m_deinterlaceLoggedFirstFrame` member gates
both messages to fire once per enable, not every frame; reset alongside
every place `m_deinterlacer` itself is reset/reconstructed (mode off, end
of stream, seek, mode change) so re-enabling logs again. Purely additive
diagnostics -- no behavior change to the deinterlacing itself.

